The following example shows how to solve a common style problem: true centering.

To achieve true centering, set both thejustify-contentand thealign-itemsproperties tocenterfor the flex container, and the flex item will be perfectly centered 
both horizontally and vertically:

### Code Snippets

```
.flex-container {
display: flex;
height: 200px;
align-items: center;
}

---

.flex-container {
display: flex;
height: 200px;
align-items: flex-start;
}

---

.flex-container {
display: flex;
height: 200px;
align-items: flex-end;
}

---

.flex-container {
display: flex;
height: 200px;
align-items: stretch;
}

---

.flex-container {
display: flex;
height: 400px;
flex-wrap: wrap;
align-content: center;
}

---

.flex-container {
display: flex;
height: 400px;
flex-wrap: wrap;
align-content: space-between;
}

---

.flex-container {
display: flex;
height: 400px;
justify-content: 
  center;
align-items: center;
}
